triage: fix_game: The rules say an illegal or unparseable reply counts as PASS, so nothing should change. When the test sent an unusable reply, the game resolved it to 'draw' and seat 1 drew a card (hand 1 to 2, draw pile 36 to 35). The likely cause is that the offer list is ['draw','points'] with no pass option, so the engine's fallback picked the first legal option.
